  "Joel.4.16.2-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.02.16, number: 3 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Joel 4:16.2</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Joel 4:16.2</h1>\n  <h2>Add note 'c' to tsadi with unexpected dagesh.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/images/2022.02.16/3-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                   This is the sole occurence in the LC where this word, מציון, \n                       is vocalized as מִצִּיּ֣וֹן. \n                   That is, the tsadi has a dagesh.\n                   All other occurences have no dagesh in the tsadi.\n                   The Miqra according to the Masorah (MAM) has a dagesh in the tsadi.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes.xml?2022.02.16-3\">2022.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2022.02.16-3</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
